# Cloudflare Workers static-asset headers.
#
# Read by Cloudflare, not by the app: Workers parses this file out of the
# deployed asset directory and applies the rules to static asset responses
# instead of the default `Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`
# (see https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/headers/). The
# file itself is never served.
#
# What each rule covers, and why a year is honest for it:
#
#   /_next/static/*  Build output. Every filename in it carries a content hash
#                    (`5865-9731a8f27c0b510b.js`), so the URL changes whenever
#                    the bytes do — that is exactly the case `immutable` exists
#                    for, and it is what Next itself sends when it serves these
#                    files. Without it, a returning visitor revalidates every
#                    chunk on every navigation.
#
#   /inspection/*    The guided-inspection card artwork: the master files plus
#                    the 585w and 1170w WebP re-encodes the homepage serves. A
#                    card's pixels are fixed by the file it names, so a change
#                    to the artwork is a change to the filename. Nothing in this
#                    directory is generated per request.
#
# Security headers are deliberately NOT repeated here. They are set for every
# response the app serves, in lib/security/headers.ts, because that is where a
# rule holds for HTML and assets alike; splitting them across two files is how
# one of them silently stops being sent.

/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/inspection/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
